body:
Maybe this is a duplicate of https://github.com/eslint/espree/issues/10 if that is the case, please feel free to close this issue :)

Here is a simple js file:

``` es6
import foo from 'foo';
```

When I run eslint (0.16.0 or master) with the default parser and this .eslintrc config:

```
{
    "rules": {
        "quotes": [1, "single"],
        "no-unused-vars": 1
    },
    "ecmaFeatures": {
        "modules": true,
    },
}
```

I get the following error:

```

/home/fabricio/bug/node_modules/eslint/node_modules/escope/escope.js:73
            throw new Error(text);
                  ^
Error
    at assert (/home/fabricio/bug/node_modules/eslint/node_modules/escope/escope.js:73:19)
    at Referencer.extend.ImportDeclaration (/home/fabricio/bug/node_modules/eslint/node_modules/escope/escope.js:1383:13)
    at Referencer.Visitor.visit (/home/fabricio/bug/node_modules/eslint/node_modules/escope/node_modules/esrecurse/esrecurse.js:109:34)
    at Referencer.Visitor.visitChildren (/home/fabricio/bug/node_modules/eslint/node_modules/escope/node_modules/esrecurse/esrecurse.js:88:38)
    at Referencer.extend.Program (/home/fabricio/bug/node_modules/eslint/node_modules/escope/escope.js:1236:18)
    at Referencer.Visitor.visit (/home/fabricio/bug/node_modules/eslint/node_modules/escope/node_modules/esrecurse/esrecurse.js:109:34)
    at Object.analyze (/home/fabricio/bug/node_modules/eslint/node_modules/escope/escope.js:1430:20)
    at EventEmitter.module.exports.api.verify (/home/fabricio/bug/node_modules/eslint/lib/eslint.js:651:35)
    at processFile (/home/fabricio/bug/node_modules/eslint/lib/cli-engine.js:193:27)
    at /home/fabricio/bug/node_modules/eslint/lib/cli-engine.js:293:26

```

The same happens if the .eslintrc is:

```
{
    "rules": {
        "quotes": [1, "single"],
        "no-unused-vars": 1
    },
    "env":{
        "es6": true
    },
    "ecmaFeatures": {
        "modules": true
    }
}
```
